  "mechanism_conclusions": [
    "SM16/112 and SM32/96 allocations are verified by CUPTI Kernel.greenContextId -> Green context metadata and driver-queried actual_resources. All ordinary kernel contextId values are 1, so ordinary contextId would not prove partitioning. Counts denote eligibility, not occupancy.",
    "Full -> SM16: AE kernel busy time increases 33.145 to 48.715 ms, but its kernel envelope falls 56.319 to 49.177 ms; nonkernel gaps fall 23.174 to 0.462 ms. Actual AE x VLM intersection increases 9.191 to 34.124 ms. This supports less scheduling/resource interference while individual AE execution uses fewer SMs; it is a profile mechanism comparison, not a steady latency estimate.",
    "SM32: all eight AE last kernels finish before VLM last kernel by 0.477 to 1.571 ms (mean 0.848 ms). AE x VLM intersection is 37.484 ms, but AE x next Vision is zero because next Vision begins after VLM finishes. The final-step frontier is 16 or 17 instead of 18, so zero exposed AE is not automatically a better freshness/quality condition.",
    "SM16 profile next Vision overlap is zero, with next Encoder starting 31.272 ms after VLM by profile Events. Non-profile formal paired repeats place it only 0.00946/0.00326 ms after VLM and Encoder ends 3.798/3.811 ms before AE. The profiler case therefore does not establish zero steady-state next Encoder overlap.",
    "Full profile next Encoder ends 1.788 ms after AE on average; non-profile paired repeats place it 12.291/12.343 ms before AE. Near-aligned profile endpoints must not be advertised as steady-state alignment.",
    "SM32 non-profile exploratory screen (20 pairs, 160 paired requests) also has no exposed AE, with AE ending about 1.943 ms before VLM and next Encoder ending about 14.215 ms after AE. This supports the mechanism, but is not the 100-pair selected-candidate confirmation.",
    "CUDA Event deltas from the matching profile result agree closely with kernel endpoint deltas; nsys export contains zero populated device Event timestamps, so no direct nsys Event timestamp validation is claimed.",
    "Six private Graph pools are supported by matching frozen constructor source hashes, explicit uniqueness checks, and passed runs. Allocator pool IDs are not directly observable in these nsys exports."
  ]
}
